---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ScrollReveal from "../../components/ScrollReveal";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Our Story"
  description="The story of Cherries Children School Foundation (CCSF) — a child-focused organisation founded to improve learning opportunities, dignity, and long-term development for children with Special Educational Needs in Rivers State, Nigeria."
>
  <section class="bg-pine-900 text-cream-100 py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl mb-4">Our Story</h1>
      <p class="font-body text-cream-100/80">Founded to build systems of support around children with Special Educational Needs.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ScrollReveal client:visible>
  <section class="bg-cream-100 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-6">
      <p class="font-body text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        Cherries Children School Foundation (CCSF) is a child-focused organization committed to improving the lives, learning opportunities, dignity, inclusion, and long-term development of children with Special Educational Needs (SEN).
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        The Foundation works to create environments in which children with special educational needs are supported to learn, develop, participate, and achieve their full potential. CCSF recognizes that meaningful inclusion requires more than access to education. It requires coordinated educational support, therapy, family participation, advocacy, community engagement, child protection, and collaboration among schools, families, healthcare professionals, government institutions, and other relevant stakeholders.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        CCSF adopts a child-centred and inclusive approach that responds to the individual strengths and needs of every child while promoting dignity, respect, equal opportunity, and lifelong development. The Foundation is guided by strong principles of good governance, accountability, safety, ethical leadership, professionalism, responsible stewardship, and compliance with applicable laws and regulatory requirements.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  </ScrollReveal>

  <ScrollReveal client:visible>
  <section class="bg-cream-200 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-pine-900 mb-4">Founders</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        Cherries Children School Foundation (CCSF) was founded by Williams Monty West and Ella William-West, whose professional backgrounds reflect the Foundation's commitment to inclusive, child-centred education and support for children with Special Educational Needs (SEN).
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-6">
        <div class="bg-cream-100 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-pine-900 mb-1">Williams Monty West</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-ink/70">Neuroeducator</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-cream-100 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-pine-900 mb-1">Ella William-West</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-ink/70">Communicologist and Inclusive Education Advocate</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  </ScrollReveal>

  <ScrollReveal client:visible>
  <section class="bg-cream-100 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-pine-900 mb-4">Registered and Recognised</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        CCSF is registered in Nigeria as an incorporated trustee/corporate body with the Corporate Affairs Commission, registered on 5 February 2024 under CAC Registration Number 7332638. The Foundation is not-for-profit and non-political, with its registered office at 15, Uyo Street, Rumuomasi, Port Harcourt, Rivers State, Nigeria.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  </ScrollReveal>
</SiteLayout>
